{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5513673","formula":"C₁₈H₃₁N₅O₆","hill":"C18H31N5O6","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":18.0,"H":31.0,"N":5.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Rapastinel"},"descriptions":{"en":"Rapastinel (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name) (former developmental code name GLYX-13) is a novel antidepressant that was under development by Allergan (previously Naurex) as an adjunctive therapy for the treatment of treatment-resistant depression. It is a centrally active, intravenously administered (non-orally active) amidated tetrapeptide that acts as a novel and selective modulator of the NMDA receptor. The drug is a rapid-acting and long-lasting antidepressant as well as robust cognitive enhancer by virtue of its ability to enhance NMDA receptor-mediated signal transduction and synaptic plasticity."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":14539800,"mass":413.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H]([C@@H](C(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1C(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N)N)O","inchikey":"GIBQQARAXHVEGD-BSOLPCOYSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-1-[(2S)-1-[(2S,3R)-2-amino-3-hydroxybutanoyl]pyrrolidine-2-carbonyl]-N-[(2S,3R)-1-amino-3-hydroxy-1-oxobutan-2-yl]pyrrolidine-2-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"14539800","atoms":60,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.671,"y":-0.454,"z":-0.476,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.438,"y":1.256,"z":-0.986,"el":"O"},{"x":3.425,"y":0.523,"z":1.579,"el":"O"},{"x":4.117,"y":-2.439,"z":1.499,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.883,"y":-2.811,"z":0.934,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.743,"y":0.168,"z":0.945,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.195,"y":1.483,"z":0.451,"el":"N"},{"x":3.09,"y":0.596,"z":-0.709,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.139,"y":-0.528,"z":0.335,"el":"N"},{"x":5.928,"y":-0.167,"z":1.234,"el":"N"},{"x":-6.266,"y":0.0,"z":-1.285,"el":"N"},{"x":1.966,"y":1.524,"z":-0.683,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.342,"y